<div class="band band--cream">
<article class="wrap-narrow dropcap">
  <header class="landing-hero">
    <p class="subtitle">Coming when it's ready</p>
    <h1 class="display">Grandma Rose's Classic Midwestern Cookbook</h1>
    <div class="landing-hero__mockup">{% svg "cookbook-mockup" %}</div>
    <p class="byline byline--muted">Assembled by the family, for the family</p>
  </header>

  <p>A bound edition of every recipe on the site. Rose's tin box, gathered into one book. Kitchen notes in the margins, seasonal chapters, and the family stories that go with the cards. Coming when it's ready.</p>

  <div class="hero__actions" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:2rem;">
    <a class="btn" href="#waitlist"><span>Join the waitlist</span></a>
  </div>
  <p class="form-note center">Launch expected 2027. The list is small and quiet. Join early.</p>
</article>
</div>

<div class="band band--linen">
<section class="wrap-narrow">
  <div class="section-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">What's inside</p>
    <h2>The book itself</h2>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li>Every recipe on this site, cleaned up and set in one place.</li>
    <li>A section of Rose's cards that never made it online, still being scanned.</li>
    <li>Kitchen notes from the margins. Substitutions, timings, and small warnings only a cook who'd made a recipe a hundred times would write down.</li>
    <li>A short chapter on cooking with what the season gives you in Ohio, month by month.</li>
    <li>A conversion chart for the old measurements Rose used ("a good pinch," "the size of a walnut").</li>
  </ul>

  <div style="margin: 2.5rem auto 0; max-width: 480px; color: var(--terracotta);">
    {% svg "cookbook-spread" %}
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<div class="band band--cream">
<section class="wrap-narrow">
  <div class="section-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Two ways to have it</p>
    <h2>Formats</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="format-grid">
    <div class="card format-card">
      <h3>Digital edition</h3>
      <p class="price">$—</p>
      <p class="price-note">Final pricing at launch. PDF and ePub.</p>
      <p>Instant download the day the book is ready. Search, bookmark, and read on any device. Free updates when the book is revised.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card format-card">
      <h3>Print edition</h3>
      <p class="price">$—</p>
      <p class="price-note">Final pricing at launch. Hardcover, print on demand.</p>
      <p>Bound hardcover, sewn spine, printed and shipped from a small press. The kind of book that lives on the counter.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<div class="band band--linen">
<section class="wrap-narrow">
  <div class="section-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">In their own words</p>
    <h2>From the family</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="quote-slider" data-slider aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Family testimonials">
    <div class="quote-slider__track" data-slider-track>
      <blockquote class="quote-slide" data-slide aria-hidden="false">
        <p class="quote-slide__mark" aria-hidden="true">“</p>
        <p class="quote-slide__text">Rose fed half the county at some point or another. Having every one of her recipes in one place is going to save me every Christmas.</p>
        <cite class="quote-slide__cite">A niece, Ohio</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="quote-slide" data-slide aria-hidden="true">
        <p class="quote-slide__mark" aria-hidden="true">“</p>
        <p class="quote-slide__text">My mother made the party potatoes for every funeral dinner. I've been trying to guess the amount of sour cream for years.</p>
        <cite class="quote-slide__cite">A cousin, Indiana</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="quote-slide" data-slide aria-hidden="true">
        <p class="quote-slide__mark" aria-hidden="true">“</p>
        <p class="quote-slide__text">The margin notes are the whole book. That's where the cooking actually lives.</p>
        <cite class="quote-slide__cite">A grandson</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="quote-slider__controls">
      <button type="button" class="quote-slider__arrow" data-slider-prev aria-label="Previous quote">‹</button>
      <div class="quote-slider__dots" data-slider-dots role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a quote"></div>
      <button type="button" class="quote-slider__arrow" data-slider-next aria-label="Next quote">›</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<div class="band band--cream">
<section class="wrap-narrow">
  <div class="section-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Why we're making it</p>
    <h2>The story behind the book</h2>
  </div>
  <p>The tin box that held Rose's recipes is starting to show its age. Some of the cards are fifty years old and older, written in pencil, folded and refolded until the creases split. The family agreed a long time ago that these should not be allowed to disappear.</p>
  <p>The site is one half of the answer. A cookbook you can hold in your hand and set on the counter is the other. If you'd like a copy when it lands, leave your email below and we'll send word.</p>

  <div class="cookbook-cta" style="margin-top:2.5rem;text-align:left;">
    <p class="cookbook-cta__eyebrow">Early subscribers get</p>
    <p style="margin:0;">A free digital sampler a few weeks before launch, a note in the acknowledgments if you'd like one, and a first-week discount code when the store opens.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<div class="band band--linen">
<section class="wrap-narrow">
  <div class="section-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Answers to what people ask</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <details><summary>When will the cookbook be out?</summary>
      <p>The working target is 2027. We'll send everyone on the waitlist the date as soon as it's locked.</p>
    </details>
    <details><summary>Will the recipes stay free on the site?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Every recipe here stays free to read, print, and share. The cookbook is for people who want them bound in one place with the extras.</p>
    </details>
    <details><summary>Do digital buyers get updates?</summary>
      <p>Yes. If we add recipes or fix an error after publication, digital buyers get the updated file at no charge.</p>
    </details>
    <details><summary>Where do you ship the print edition?</summary>
      <p>The print partner ships anywhere they can reach at reasonable rates. We'll list the country list at launch.</p>
    </details>
    <details><summary>Refund policy on the digital edition?</summary>
      <p>Full refund within 30 days if you decide it isn't for you, no questions.</p>
    </details>
    <details><summary>Can I gift the cookbook?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Digital gifting will be a checkbox at checkout. Print copies can ship straight to the giftee.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

<div class="band band--cream">
<section class="wrap-narrow" id="waitlist">
  <div class="section-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Leave your email</p>
    <h2>Join the waitlist</h2>
  </div>
  <form class="waitlist" action="{{ site.waitlist.endpoint }}" method="post">
    <div class="form-row">
      <label for="email">Email</label>
      <input type="email" name="email" id="email" required placeholder="you@example.com">
    </div>
    <div class="form-row">
      <label for="first_name">First name (optional)</label>
      <input type="text" name="first_name" id="first_name" placeholder="For a friendlier launch email">
    </div>
    <div class="form-row">
      <label>What are you most interested in?</label>
      <div class="checkbox-group">
        <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="digital"> Digital edition</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="print"> Print edition</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="both"> Both</label>
      </div>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="btn"><span>Join the waitlist</span></button>
    <p class="form-note">We'll use your email only to let you know when the cookbook is ready. Unsubscribe any time.</p>
  </form>
</section>
</div>
